From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:36:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a text sized to its lines from being cut to none

A multiline text extra aligned to the top is cut to its whole lines on
screen. Its height, made from its lines when the theme gives it none,
is a fraction of a pixel more than the rounded rectangle on screen,
which then held one line less than it has: a one-line title in a stack
was cut to nothing. The cut keeps the lines the box holds within a
pixel, and at least one.
---
 es-core/src/components/TextComponent.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/es-core/src/components/TextComponent.cpp b/es-core/src/components/TextComponent.cpp
index ac6c48b4..7b16fb0d 100644
--- a/es-core/src/components/TextComponent.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/components/TextComponent.cpp
@@ -173,11 +173,11 @@ void TextComponent::render(const Transform4x4f& parentTrans)
 	{
 		if (mExtraType == ExtraType::EXTRACHILDREN && mVerticalAlignment == Alignment::ALIGN_TOP && mMultiline == MultiLineType::MULTILINE && mAutoScroll == AutoScrollType::NONE)
 		{
-			// Clip multiline - non partial lines
+			// Clip multiline - non partial lines (a box made as tall as its lines, then rounded on screen, keeps them)
 			auto lineHeight = mFont->getHeight(mLineSpacing);
 			if (lineHeight > 0)
 			{
-				auto lines = (int)(rect.h / lineHeight);
+				auto lines = std::max(1, (int)((rect.h + 1) / lineHeight));
 				rect.h = lineHeight * lines + 1;
 			}
 
